Your regex `[0-9]+` is actually FINE for extracting digits — the problem is you're not anchoring it between the delimiters, so it matches ANY digits in the string, including ones outside your markers.

You need a pattern that REQUIRES the delimiters around the digits. Something like:

```cpp
#include <regex>
#include <string>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::string text = "[Delimter1]abc123[delimter2]";
    std::regex re(R"(\[Delimter1\].*?(\d+).*?\[delimter2\])");
    std::smatch m;
    if (std::regex_search(text, m, re)) {
        std::cout << m[1].str();  // 123
    }
}
```

Key points:
- The capture group `(\d+)` is what you actually want.
- `.*?` is NON-greedy, so it stops at the FIRST digit run.
- Escape the brackets `\[` `\]` — otherwise they're character classes.

If the digits are ALWAYS the only thing between the delimiters, simplify to `\[Delimter1\](\d+)\[delimter2\]`.

